§ `Chapter 5 - Abetment`

-- s 107 Explanation 1, Illustration: B, knowing C is not Z, intentionally represents
-- to A (a public officer with a warrant for Z) that C is Z, and thereby intentionally
-- causes A to apprehend C. B abets by instigation the apprehension of C.
`s 107 illus` MEANS `Abetment Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `the particulars in the illustrations`
    `the person abetted` IS "A"
    `the person abetted described as` IS ""
    `the offence abetted` IS "the apprehension of C"
    `the section punishing the offence abetted` IS ""
    `the punishment provided for the offence abetted` IS ""
    `the manner of the abetment` IS ""
    `instigates any person to do that thing` IS FALSE
    `by intentional misrepresentation` IS TRUE
    `by intentional concealment of a material fact which he is bound to disclose` IS FALSE
    `voluntarily causes or procures, or attempts to cause or procure, a thing to be done` IS TRUE
    `engages with one or more other persons in a conspiracy for the doing of that thing` IS FALSE
    `an act or illegal omission takes place in pursuance of that conspiracy` IS FALSE
    `in order to the doing of that thing` IS FALSE
    `the aid is intentional` IS FALSE
    `by any act or illegal omission` IS FALSE
    `does anything, prior to or at the time of the commission of the act, in order to facilitate its commission` IS FALSE
    `thereby facilitates the commission of the act` IS FALSE
    `the thing abetted is the commission of an offence` IS FALSE
    `the thing abetted is an act which would be an offence if committed by a person capable by law of committing an offence with the same intention or knowledge as that of the abettor` IS FALSE
    `abets in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the act abetted is to be committed without and beyond Singapore and would constitute an offence if committed in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `the act abetted is committed` IS FALSE
    `in consequence of the instigation` IS FALSE
    `in pursuance of the conspiracy` IS FALSE
    `with the aid which constitutes the abetment` IS FALSE
    `that offence is not committed in consequence of the abetment` IS FALSE
    `no express provision is made by this Code for the punishment of such abetment` IS FALSE
    `no express provision is made by this Code or by any other written law for the punishment of such abetment` IS FALSE
    `the offence abetted is punishable with death or imprisonment for life` IS FALSE
    `the offence abetted is punishable with imprisonment` IS FALSE
    `abets the commission of the offence by the public generally` IS FALSE
    `abets the commission of the offence by a number or class of persons exceeding 10` IS FALSE
    `a different act is done` IS FALSE
    `the act done was a probable consequence of the abetment` IS FALSE
    `the act done was committed under the influence of the instigation, or with the aid or in pursuance of the conspiracy which constituted the abetment` IS FALSE
    `the act done is committed in addition to the act abetted` IS FALSE
    `the act done constitutes a distinct offence` IS FALSE
    `the act is abetted with the intention of causing a particular effect` IS FALSE
    `the act causes a different effect from that intended by the abettor` IS FALSE
    `the abettor knew that the act abetted was likely to cause that effect` IS FALSE
    `is present when the act or offence is committed` IS FALSE
