-- s 107 Explanation 1 Illustration: "B abets by instigation the apprehension of C"
#ASSERT `instigates within section 107` `s 107 illus`
#ASSERT `abets the doing of a thing` `s 107 illus`

-- s 108 Explanation 2 Illustration (a): "A is guilty of abetting B to commit murder"
#ASSERT `abets an offence` `s 108 illus (a)`
-- ... murder was not committed, so not s 109; s 115 (murder is punishable with death)
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 109` `s 108 illus (a)`)
#ASSERT `offence under s 115` `s 108 illus (a)`
-- s 108 Explanation 2 Illustration (b): "A is guilty of instigating B to commit murder"
#ASSERT `abets an offence` `s 108 illus (b)`
#ASSERT `offence under s 115` `s 108 illus (b)`

-- s 108 Explanation 3 Illustration (a): "A, whether the act is committed or not, is guilty of abetting an offence"
#ASSERT `abets an offence` `s 108 Expl 3 illus (a)`
-- s 108 Explanation 3 Illustration (b): "A is liable to be punished in the same manner as if B ... had committed murder"
#ASSERT `offence under s 109` `s 108 Expl 3 illus (b)`
-- s 108 Explanation 3 Illustration (d): "A is guilty of abetting theft, and is liable to the same punishment as if B had committed theft"
#ASSERT `offence under s 109` `s 108 Expl 3 illus (d)`
-- s 108 Explanation 4 Illustration: "A is also liable to the same punishment"
#ASSERT `offence under s 109` `s 108 Expl 4 illus`
-- s 108 Explanation 5 Illustration: "C has therefore committed the offence defined in this section, and is liable to the punishment for murder"
#ASSERT `abets the doing of a thing` `s 108 Expl 5 illus`
#ASSERT `offence under s 109` `s 108 Expl 5 illus`
-- s 108A Illustration: "A is guilty of abetting murder"
#ASSERT `abets an offence` `s 108A illus`
-- s 108B: an abetment from abroad of an offence in Singapore is still an abetment
#ASSERT `abets an offence` `s 108B, abetment from abroad`

-- s 109 Illustration (a): "A has abetted the offence defined in section 161"
#ASSERT `offence under s 109` `s 109 illus (a)`
-- s 109 Illustration (b): "A is guilty of abetting that offence, and is liable to the same punishment as B"
#ASSERT `offence under s 109` `s 109 illus (b)`
-- s 109 Illustration (c): "A is guilty of abetting that offence by conspiracy, and is liable to the punishment for murder"
#ASSERT `offence under s 109` `s 109 illus (c)`

-- s 111 Illustration (a): "A is liable in the same manner, and to the same extent, as if he had instigated the child to put the poison into the food of Y"
#ASSERT `liable for the act done within section 111` `s 111 illus (a)`
-- s 111 Illustration (b): "A ... is not guilty of abetting the theft"
#ASSERT NOT (`liable for the act done within section 111` `s 111 illus (b)`)
-- s 111 Illustration (c): "if that murder was the probable consequence of the abetment, A is liable to the punishment provided for murder"
#ASSERT `liable for the act done within section 111` `s 111 illus (c)`
-- s 112 Illustration: "A will also be liable to punishment for each of the offences"
#ASSERT `liable for each of the offences within section 112` `s 112 illus`
-- s 113 Illustration: "if A knew that the grievous hurt abetted was likely to cause death, A is liable to be punished with the punishment provided for murder"
#ASSERT `liable for the effect caused within section 113` `s 113 illus`
#ASSERT NOT (`liable for the effect caused within section 113` `s 113 illus, not known`)
-- s 114: present, so deemed to have committed the offence
#ASSERT `deemed to have committed the offence within section 114` `s 114, present`

-- s 115 Illustration: "A shall be punished with imprisonment for a term that may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
#ASSERT `offence under s 115` `s 115 illus`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 115` `s 115 illus`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term that may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 115` `s 115 illus`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2026, at Block 1 Orchard Road, Singapore, did abet the commission of murder by instigating one B, to wit, by offering him $10,000 to kill one Z, an offence punishable under section 302 with death or imprisonment for life, which offence was not committed in consequence of your abetment, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 115 of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT NOT (`punishable with death or imprisonment for life` `punishment prescribed by s 115`)
#ASSERT `punishable with imprisonment for` 240 `months or upwards within section 41` `punishment prescribed by s 115`
-- s 115 is the express provision s 116's proviso excludes: an abetment of murder not
-- committed is s 115, not s 116 (FORK GP-13)
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 116` `s 115 illus`)
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 116` `s 108 illus (a)`)
-- s 115 and s 109 are exclusive on the facts: murder committed is s 109
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 115` `s 109 illus (c)`)

-- s 116 Illustration (a): "A is punishable under this section for abetting the offence in section 161"
#ASSERT `offence under s 116` `s 116 illus (a)`
-- s 116 Illustration (b): "if B does not give false evidence, A has nevertheless committed the offence defined in this section"
#ASSERT `offence under s 116` `s 109 illus (b), not committed`
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 109` `s 109 illus (b), not committed`)
-- s 116 Illustration (c): "though the robbery is not committed, A is liable to the maximum term of imprisonment provided for that offence"
#ASSERT `offence under s 116` `s 116 illus (c)`
#ASSERT (`the punishment under s 116 for abetting an offence punishable with` `s 392 punishment`)'s `maximum term in months` EQUALS (`s 392 punishment`'s `maximum term in months`)
-- s 116 Illustration (d): "B is liable to the same punishment as if he had committed the offence of robbery"
#ASSERT `offence under s 116` `s 116 illus (d)`
-- s 116(2)-(3) over robbery's punishment: minimum terms and strokes go; no fine appears (s 116(3))
#ASSERT (`the punishment under s 116 for abetting an offence punishable with` `s 392 punishment`)'s `minimum term in months` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`the punishment under s 116 for abetting an offence punishable with` `s 392 punishment`)'s `minimum strokes` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`the punishment under s 116 for abetting an offence punishable with` `s 392 punishment`)'s `maximum term in months` EQUALS JUST 120
#ASSERT (`the punishment under s 116 for abetting an offence punishable with` `s 392 punishment`)'s fine EQUALS `not prescribed`
#ASSERT (`the punishment under s 116 for abetting an offence punishable with` `s 392 punishment`)'s caning EQUALS `or with`
-- ... and an offence with no minimum keeps its punishment, relabelled
#ASSERT (`the punishment under s 116 for abetting an offence punishable with` `s 379 punishment`)'s words EQUALS (`s 379 punishment`'s words)
#ASSERT (`the punishment under s 116 for abetting an offence punishable with` `s 379 punishment`)'s section EQUALS "379 read with 116"
#ASSERT (`the punishment under s 109 for abetting an offence punishable with` `s 379 punishment`)'s section EQUALS "379 read with 109"

-- s 117 Illustration: "A has committed an offence under this section"
#ASSERT `offence under s 117` `s 117 illus`
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 117` `s 117, ten workers`)
#ASSERT `exceeding 10` 11
#ASSERT NOT (`exceeding 10` 10)

-- s 107(1)(c) with Explanation 2
#ASSERT `abets the doing of a thing` `s 107(1)(c), aid`
#ASSERT `offence under s 109` `s 107(1)(c), aid`
#ASSERT NOT (`abets the doing of a thing` `s 107(1)(c), aid that did not facilitate`)

-- The s 109 charge, as text (a charge "read with section 109")
#ASSERT (`charge under s 109` `s 109 illus (b)`)'s `made out`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 109` `s 109 illus (b)`)'s section EQUALS "193 read with 109"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 109` `s 109 illus (b)`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2026, at Block 1 Orchard Road, Singapore, did abet the commission of giving false evidence by instigating one B, a witness, to wit, by asking him to testify that he saw Z at the scene, which offence was committed in consequence of your abetment, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 193 read with section 109 of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 109` `s 107(1)(c), aid`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2026, at Block 1 Orchard Road, Singapore, did abet the commission of theft by intentionally aiding one B, which offence was committed in consequence of your abetment, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 379 read with section 109 of the Penal Code 1871."
-- ... and the refusal, when nothing was done to abet
#ASSERT NOT ((`charge under s 109` `no abetment`)'s `made out`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 109` `no abetment`)'s text EQUALS ""
#ASSERT (`charge under s 109` `no abetment`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 379 read with section 109 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of abetment of theft (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: instigates any person to do that thing, engages in a conspiracy for its doing, or intentionally aids its doing (section 107); the elements of sections 107 and 108 taken together."
-- the s 116 charge, when the false evidence was not given
#ASSERT (`charge under s 116` `s 109 illus (b), not committed`)'s section EQUALS "193 read with 116"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 116` `s 109 illus (b), not committed`)'s `made out`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 117` `s 117 illus`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2026, at Block 1 Orchard Road, Singapore, did abet the commission of mischief by a number or class of persons exceeding 10, to wit, by affixing a placard at the worksite calling on the workers to damage property there, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 117 of the Penal Code 1871."
-- s 118 Illustration: A, knowing that a gang-robbery is about to be committed at B,
-- falsely informs the police that one is about to be committed at C, and thereby misleads
-- the police with intent to facilitate the offence. The gang-robbery is committed at B.
-- A is punishable under this section. (The Illustration treats gang-robbery as an
-- offence punishable with death or imprisonment for life.)
`s 118 illus` MEANS `Concealment of Design Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `the particulars in the illustrations`
    `the offence designed` IS "gang-robbery"
    `the section punishing the offence designed` IS "395"
    `the design` IS "to commit gang-robbery at B"
    `the manner of the concealment` IS "by falsely informing the police that a gang-robbery was about to be committed at C"
    `intending to facilitate the commission of the offence` IS TRUE
    `knowing it to be likely that he will thereby facilitate the commission of the offence` IS FALSE
    voluntarily IS FALSE
    `conceals, by any act or illegal omission, the existence of a design to commit the offence` IS FALSE
    `makes a representation which he knows to be false respecting the design` IS TRUE
    `the offence designed is punishable with death or imprisonment for life` IS TRUE
    `the offence designed is punishable with imprisonment` IS TRUE
    `the offence designed is committed` IS TRUE
    `being a public servant` IS FALSE
    `the commission of the offence is his duty as such public servant to prevent` IS FALSE
