-- s 118 Illustration: "A is punishable under this section"
#ASSERT `offence under s 118` `s 118 illus`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 118` `s 118 illus`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 7 years ... and, in either case, shall also be liable to fine"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 118` `s 118 illus`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2026, at Block 1 Orchard Road, Singapore, did, intending to facilitate the commission of gang-robbery, an offence punishable under section 395, make a representation which you knew to be false respecting a design to commit gang-robbery at B, to wit, by falsely informing the police that a gang-robbery was about to be committed at C, which offence was committed, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 118 of the Penal Code 1871."
-- FINDING (FORK GP-14): the s 118 Illustration says "A is punishable under this section",
-- but gang-robbery as s 395 now punishes it is not punishable with death or imprisonment
-- for life. This assertion is the Illustration's conclusion on the Code's current s 395;
-- it is EXPECTED TO FAIL, and is left failing.
#ASSERT `offence under s 118` `s 118 illus, gang-robbery as s 395 now punishes it`
-- ... on those facts it is s 120 that applies
#ASSERT `offence under s 120` `s 118 illus, gang-robbery as s 395 now punishes it`
