-- one-eighth and one-fourth of theft's 3 years; one-half of robbery's 10
#ASSERT `the fraction` (1/8) `of the longest term provided for` `s 379 punishment` EQUALS 4.5
#ASSERT `the fraction` (1/4) `of the longest term provided for` `s 379 punishment` EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `the fraction` (1/2) `of the longest term provided for` `s 392 punishment` EQUALS 60
-- a fraction of imprisonment for life is refused by name; see it with #EVAL
#EVAL `the fraction` (1/4) `of the longest term provided for` `s 364 punishment`

§ `Chapter 5A - Criminal conspiracy`

-- A agrees with B to cheat a bank. No express provision punishes the conspiracy.
`s 120A, an agreement to cheat` MEANS `Criminal Conspiracy Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `the particulars in the illustrations`
    `the other party` IS "one B"
    `the offence agreed upon` IS "cheating"
    `the section punishing the offence agreed upon` IS "420"
    `the agreement` IS "to deceive DBS Bank into releasing a loan of $50,000"
    `agrees with another person` IS TRUE
    `to commit an offence` IS TRUE
    `to cause an offence to be committed` IS FALSE
    `is a party in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `to commit an act outside Singapore which would constitute an offence if committed in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `no express provision is made in this Code for the punishment of such a conspiracy` IS TRUE
-- A, in Singapore, agrees with B to commit abroad an act that would be cheating here.
`s 120A(4), an agreement for abroad` MEANS `Criminal Conspiracy Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `the particulars in the illustrations`
    `the other party` IS "one B"
    `the offence agreed upon` IS "cheating"
    `the section punishing the offence agreed upon` IS "420"
    `the agreement` IS ""
    `agrees with another person` IS TRUE
    `to commit an offence` IS FALSE
    `to cause an offence to be committed` IS FALSE
    `is a party in Singapore` IS TRUE
    `to commit an act outside Singapore which would constitute an offence if committed in Singapore` IS TRUE
    `no express provision is made in this Code for the punishment of such a conspiracy` IS TRUE
-- B proposes the cheat; A never agrees.
`s 120A, no agreement` MEANS `Criminal Conspiracy Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `the particulars in the illustrations`
    `the other party` IS "one B"
    `the offence agreed upon` IS "cheating"
    `the section punishing the offence agreed upon` IS "420"
    `the agreement` IS ""
    `agrees with another person` IS FALSE
    `to commit an offence` IS TRUE
    `to cause an offence to be committed` IS FALSE
    `is a party in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `to commit an act outside Singapore which would constitute an offence if committed in Singapore` IS FALSE
    `no express provision is made in this Code for the punishment of such a conspiracy` IS TRUE

#ASSERT `is a party to a criminal conspiracy` `s 120A, an agreement to cheat`
#ASSERT `offence under s 120B` `s 120A, an agreement to cheat`
#ASSERT `is a party to a criminal conspiracy` `s 120A(4), an agreement for abroad`
#ASSERT NOT (`is a party to a criminal conspiracy` `s 120A, no agreement`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 120B` `s 120A, an agreement to cheat`)'s section EQUALS "120B read with 420"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 120B` `s 120A, an agreement to cheat`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2026, at Block 1 Orchard Road, Singapore, were a party to a criminal conspiracy with one B to commit cheating, to wit, to deceive DBS Bank into releasing a loan of $50,000, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 120B read with section 420 of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 120B` `s 120A, no agreement`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 120B read with section 420 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of criminal conspiracy to commit cheating (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: agrees with another person; the elements of section 120A taken together."

§ `Chapter 23 - Attempts`

-- s 511 Illustration (a): A breaks open a box to steal jewels and finds none. He has
-- taken a substantial step towards theft, and is guilty of attempted theft.
`s 511 illus (a)` MEANS `Attempt Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `the particulars in the illustrations`
    `the offence attempted` IS "theft"
    `the particulars of the attempt` IS "of some jewels, by breaking open a box"
    `the section punishing the offence attempted` IS "379"
    `the punishment prescribed for the offence attempted` IS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both"
    `the offence is punishable by this Code or by any other written law` IS TRUE
    `with the intention of committing that offence` IS TRUE
    `does an act towards the commission of that offence` IS TRUE
    `the act is strongly corroborative of an intention to commit the offence` IS TRUE
    `the offence attempted is punishable with death or imprisonment for life` IS FALSE
    `no express provision is made for the punishment of such attempt` IS TRUE
    `the punishment prescribed for the offence is fixed by law or a minimum sentence` IS FALSE
