-- s 512(1) Illustration: A attempts to kidnap B in order that B may be murdered, and
-- fails. Kidnapping in order to murder (s 364) is punishable with death or imprisonment
-- for life. A shall be punished with imprisonment up to 20 years, and shall also be
-- liable to fine or to caning.
`s 512(1) illus` MEANS `Attempt Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `the particulars in the illustrations`
    `the offence attempted` IS "kidnapping in order to murder"
    `the particulars of the attempt` IS ""
    `the section punishing the offence attempted` IS "364"
    `the punishment prescribed for the offence attempted` IS ""
    `the offence is punishable by this Code or by any other written law` IS TRUE
    `with the intention of committing that offence` IS TRUE
    `does an act towards the commission of that offence` IS TRUE
    `the act is strongly corroborative of an intention to commit the offence` IS TRUE
    `the offence attempted is punishable with death or imprisonment for life` IS `punishable with death or imprisonment for life` `s 364 punishment`
    `no express provision is made for the punishment of such attempt` IS TRUE
    `the punishment prescribed for the offence is fixed by law or a minimum sentence` IS FALSE
-- s 512(4) Illustration: A attempts robbery and does not succeed. s 393 makes express
-- provision for an attempt to commit robbery (FORK GP-10), so the leaf is FALSE here.
`s 512(4) illus` MEANS `Attempt Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `the particulars in the illustrations`
    `the offence attempted` IS "robbery"
    `the particulars of the attempt` IS ""
    `the section punishing the offence attempted` IS "392"
    `the punishment prescribed for the offence attempted` IS ""
    `the offence is punishable by this Code or by any other written law` IS TRUE
    `with the intention of committing that offence` IS TRUE
    `does an act towards the commission of that offence` IS TRUE
    `the act is strongly corroborative of an intention to commit the offence` IS TRUE
    `the offence attempted is punishable with death or imprisonment for life` IS `punishable with death or imprisonment for life` `s 392 punishment`
    `no express provision is made for the punishment of such attempt` IS FALSE
    `the punishment prescribed for the offence is fixed by law or a minimum sentence` IS `fixed by law or carries a minimum sentence` `s 392 punishment`

-- s 511 Illustrations (a)-(d): each "is guilty of attempted theft", impossibility notwithstanding (s 511(3))
#ASSERT `attempts to commit an offence` `s 511 illus (a)`
#ASSERT `offence under s 512(2)` `s 511 illus (a)`
#ASSERT `attempts to commit an offence` `s 511 illus (b)`
#ASSERT `offence under s 512(2)` `s 511 illus (b)`
#ASSERT `attempts to commit an offence` `s 511 illus (c)`
#ASSERT `offence under s 512(2)` `s 511 illus (c)`
#ASSERT `attempts to commit an offence` `s 511 illus (d)`
#ASSERT `offence under s 512(2)` `s 511 illus (d)`
-- s 511(2): not strongly corroborative, not a substantial step
#ASSERT NOT (`attempts to commit an offence` `s 511, a step not corroborative`)
-- s 512(1) Illustration
#ASSERT `offence under s 512(1)` `s 512(1) illus`
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 512(2)` `s 512(1) illus`)
#ASSERT (`charge under s 512(1)` `s 512(1) illus`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 20 years, and shall also be liable to fine or to caning"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 512(1)` `s 512(1) illus`)'s section EQUALS "364 read with 511"
-- s 512(4) Illustration, on the punishment: not bound by robbery's minimum term or
-- minimum strokes, and no fine ("the court may not sentence A to a fine")
#ASSERT (`the punishment under s 512(2) for attempting an offence punishable with` `s 392 punishment`)'s `minimum term in months` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`the punishment under s 512(2) for attempting an offence punishable with` `s 392 punishment`)'s `minimum strokes` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT (`the punishment under s 512(2) for attempting an offence punishable with` `s 392 punishment`)'s caning EQUALS `or with`
#ASSERT (`the punishment under s 512(2) for attempting an offence punishable with` `s 392 punishment`)'s imprisonment EQUALS `or with`
#ASSERT (`the punishment under s 512(2) for attempting an offence punishable with` `s 392 punishment`)'s fine EQUALS `not prescribed`
#ASSERT (`the punishment under s 512(2) for attempting an offence punishable with` `s 392 punishment`)'s `maximum term in months` EQUALS JUST 120
#ASSERT NOT (`fixed by law or carries a minimum sentence` (`the punishment under s 512(2) for attempting an offence punishable with` `s 392 punishment`))
-- s 512(4) Illustration, on the offence: s 393 expressly punishes an attempt to commit
-- robbery, so s 512(2) does not frame it (FORK GP-10)
#ASSERT NOT (`offence under s 512(2)` `s 512(4) illus`)
-- FINDING (FORK GP-10): the s 512(4) Illustration treats attempted robbery as punishable
-- under s 512(2)-(3) ("A may be sentenced to 6 months imprisonment with no caning for
-- attempted robbery"). This assertion is that conclusion on the Code's facts, where
-- s 393 makes express provision; it is EXPECTED TO FAIL, and is left failing.
#ASSERT `offence under s 512(2)` `s 512(4) illus`
-- the charge, as text, and a refusal
#ASSERT (`charge under s 512(2)` `s 511 illus (a)`)'s `made out`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 512(2)` `s 511 illus (a)`)'s section EQUALS "379 read with 511"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 512(2)` `s 511 illus (a)`)'s text EQUALS "You, A, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of March 2026, at Block 1 Orchard Road, Singapore, did attempt to commit theft of some jewels, by breaking open a box, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 379 read with section 511 of the Penal Code 1871."
#ASSERT (`charge under s 512(2)` `s 511 illus (a)`)'s punishment EQUALS "such punishment as is prescribed for that offence (imprisonment for a term which may extend to 3 years, or with fine, or with both)"
#ASSERT (`charge under s 512(2)` `s 511, a step not corroborative`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 379 read with section 511 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of attempt to commit theft (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: takes a substantial step towards the commission of that offence - an act strongly corroborative of an intention to commit it (section 511(2))."
